    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70760" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νησιωτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>from an island,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθνεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.80
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1261
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνομα νησιωτικὸν Σαλαμῖνα
				θέμενον</span> having given it the <i>island</i> name of
			Salamis, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				149
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ξενύδρια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					462.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ν.</span>”
				<i>insular situation,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.57
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλητὴρ ν.</span> a summoner <i>of
				the islanders,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1422
			</span></i>.</div>
